            <div xml:id="d467">

                <pb facs="0474" n="470" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg470"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.61331/170: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-11-17T19:00:00-05:00">November 17,
                            1939—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>359. Tsingtao’s 212, November 13, 11 a.m., and your despatch 4170 of October
                        9,<anchor n="21" xml:id="d467-f1"/> Universal Leaf Tobacco Company. The head
                    office of the company in this country has informed the Department that the
                    proposal outlined in Tsingtao’s telegram under reference is contrary to its best
                    business judgment and that it has cabled its Shanghai office “recommending that
                    they do not agree because the proposal is not only unreasonable but in our
                    opinion involves illegal restrictions”.</p>
                <p>In view of the flagrant nature of this instance of Japanese interference with
                    American business in China, the Department desires that unless you perceive
                    objection you make a further approach to the Foreign Office in regard to the
                    case and that Tsingtao continue to press appropriate Japanese authorities at
                    that port.</p>
                <p>Sent to Tokyo via Shanghai. Repeated to Tsingtao.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
